{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "27", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "05", "M": "31", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "MMDR amendment brings cost relief to Tamil Nadu cement makers", "para": "South India's cement manufacturers are breathing easier following the removal of a burdensome limestone tax by Tamil Nadu. The implementation of the MMDR Amendment Bill of 2026 has facilitated this change, promising substantial annual savings for the industry. As a direct result, the outlook for financial gains in the cement sector appears more promising than ever.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/mmdr-amendment-brings-cost-relief-to-tamil-nadu-cement-makers/133555760?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-157982/133555760.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}, {"title": "Foxconn looks for 200 acres land parcel to set up technology park, Gujarat on radar", "para": "According to top sources in govt, Foxconn executives have surveyed the plot of land near Sanand and the company will take a call on finalising the location in the coming weeks. \u201cThe company intends to set up a mobile phone and other high-end electronics manufacturing plant,\u201d a senior state govt official said, clarifying that Gujarat is not the only state being considered by the company for the new project.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/foxconn-looks-for-200-acres-land-parcel-to-set-up-technology-park-gujarat-on-radar/133555639?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-176590/133555639.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "About \u20b92,500-crore property tax arrears from merged areas squeeze Pune civic body's finances", "para": "Facing a critical financial shortfall of Rs 2,500 crore, the Pune Municipal Corporation confronts resistance to property taxes in newly incorporated suburban regions. Residents claim that the insufficient civic services provided justify their tax withholding. Adding to the dilemma, political opposition to collection efforts has created a deadlock that burdens the current city taxpayers more heavily.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/about-2500-crore-property-tax-arrears-from-merged-areas-squeeze-pune-civic-bodys-finances/133555282?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-140452/133555282.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}